<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26109" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāvīnĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Latium, near the
				sea-coast, six Roman miles distant from Laurentum, founded by
				Æneas in honor of his wife Lavinia</i>, now <i>Pratica</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 1,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 144</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">id. R. R. 2, 4, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				728</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 12, 71</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāvīnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Lavinium, Lavinian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 236</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 25</span></i> (3, 32),
			64.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāvīnĭenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, 
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Lavinium,
				Lavinians</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 4, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
